DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The arguments are:

     _v_p     The vnode being manipulated.

     _i_d     The id token which is changing the lock.

     _o_p     The operation to perform (see fcntl(2)).

     _f_l     Description of the lock.

     _f_l_a_g_s  One or more of the following:

                  F_WAIT    Wait until lock is granted.
                  F_FLOCK   Use flock(2) semantics for lock.
                  F_POSIX   Use POSIX semantics for lock.
                  F_REMOTE  Lock owner is remote NFS client.
                  F_NOINTR  Mask signals while waiting for the lock.

     This entry point manipulates advisory record locks on the file.  Most
     file systems delegate the work for this call to llff__aaddvvlloocckk().

